LANGUAGE English

// use this for both goalStopRitual and goalRescueBoy
BOOK DvmStopRitual ORDERED KEEP
    IF goal == goalStopRitual AND ritual == 0 THEN EXIT BEFORE

    PAGE Page1
        PROLOG "The {c:QItemDVM} looks old and worn with time."

        BUTTON "Read the first page" AFTER "Table of Contents"

        TEXT "
            Table of Contents

            You open the book to the first page. It's a table of contents. You
            quickly scan down and find the spell to close portals. In the
            margin, someone--probably your father--scrawled a note that reads,
            <<My descendants will be able to read this book, but only at the
            appointed hour. I have seen to this.>>

            You find <<Travel, page 72.>>

            The first time this is read, gain 1 {clue}.
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Page2
        PROLOG "
            You turn to page 72, the travel section. The first entry is for
            portals.
        "
        
        BUTTON "Read about portals" AFTER "Overview"

        TEXT "
            You read through an overview of the ritual and how to perform it.
            Some of the materials needed are a special {c:QItemDagger}, a
            chalice, a human skull, some religious icons, and various herbs.
            There's also mention of an <<{c:QItemElderSign,>> but you aren>t
            sure what that is.

            You must find the {c:QItemRitualDagger} Common Item,
            {c:QItemRitualComponents} Unique Item, and
            {c:QItemElderSignPendant} Common Item.

            <i>Maybe they don't have all of these yet</i> you think to
            yourself.
        "
    END PAGE


    PAGE Page3
        PROLOG "This ritual seems complicated."

        BUTTON "Read next page" AFTER "Tools"

        TEXT "
            The {c:QItemDagger}
        
            You flip the page. Here the book goes into detail about the
            {c:QItemDagger} needed to open the portal. You are surprised at how
            intricate the ritual is. There is also a section about blessing the
            {c:QItemDagger}, but when it gets to the actual blessing, it is
            written in a language you cannot read.

            {c:QItemElderSign}
        
            Once the portal has manifested, it is weak and unstable. An
            {c:QItemElderSign} is used to stabilize it. There is a picture of
            one here, so you at least know what it looks like now.

            Gain 1 {clue}.
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Page4
        PROLOG "Opening a portal seem complicated."

        BUTTON "Read next page" AFTER "Sacrifice"

        TEXT "
            The next page delves into the importance of personal sacrifice. For
            this ritual, the required sacrifice is large. A cold chill runs
            down your spine as you realize that only a precious loved one is
            enough. <i>What kind of monster could do such a thing?>></i> you
            ask yourself.
        
            The first time this is read, suffer 1 Horror ({will} negates), then
            gain 2 {clue} if you don’t go Insane.

        "
        
        IF journalReadPage4 THEN TEXT "
            The Sacrifice
        
            The next page delves into the importance of personal sacrifice.
            For this ritual, the required sacrifice is large. A chill runs down
            your spine as you realize that only a precious loved one is enough.
            <i>The boy from the journal,</i> you think to yourself. <i>He>s
            here somewhere and we>re going to find him.</i>
        
            The first time this is read, suffer 1 Horror ({will} negates), then
            gain 2 {clue} if you don>t go Insane.
        "

    END PAGE

    PAGE Page5
        PROLOG "
            You glance back through the pages to see if you missed anything.
        "

        BUTTON "Look through the pages again" AFTER "Incantations"

        TEXT "
            Incantations

            As you flip through the pages again, you see notice several
            incantations written in a language you cannot read. That's
            probably why you missed them the first time.

            You think back to the margin scrawl in the front of the book.
            <<Maybe {c:MonsterDavidSmythe} will be able to read these?<i>
            you wonder out loud. One of the other investigators glaces at
            you, wondering what you are talking about.
        "
    END PAGE

    EPILOG
        TEXT "
            Special tools. Unreadable incantations. Blood and sacrifice.
            
            This ritual is dark and terrible. It must not be allowed to
            succeed.
        "
    END EPILOG
END BOOK

